.TH PINFIT 1 "2026-09-21" "Pinfit" "Pinfit Manual"
.SH NAME
pinfit \- YAML\-driven C interface and module generator for embedded projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Pinfit
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Pinfit
generates C headers and sources from short YAML specs: interfaces, modules, state machines,
observers, command tables, status codes and adapters. Your own code lives in named user regions
inside the generated files and survives every regeneration.
.PP
When no native launcher is installed, substitute
.B "java \-jar pinfit.jar"
for
.B Pinfit
everywhere below.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "init " "[directory] [\-f|\-\-force]"
Create a new
.I pinfit.yaml
project file. Without a directory it writes in the current one.
It refuses to overwrite an existing
.I pinfit.yaml
unless
.B \-f
is given.
.TP
.BI "create interface " "name " "[directory]"
.TP
.BI "create module " "name " "[directory] [\-\-implements " "name[,name...]" ]
.TP
.BI "create state\-machine " "name " "[directory]"
.TP
.BI "create observer " "name " "\-\-interface " "name " "[directory] [\-\-capacity " n ]
.TP
.BI "create command\-table " "name " "[directory]"
.TP
.BI "create status\-codes " "name " "[directory]"
.TP
.BI "create adapter " "name " "\-\-from " "interface " "\-\-to " "interface " "[directory]"
Write a spec file of the given kind into
.IR directory ,
creating it when needed. Without a directory it writes in the current one.
.B create
writes YAML only; run
.B "pinfit generate"
to produce the C.
.TP
.BI "gen " "[directory] [\-f|\-\-force] [\-v|\-\-verbose] [\-\-also\-nested]"
.TP
.BI "generate " "[directory] [\-f|\-\-force] [\-v|\-\-verbose] [\-\-also\-nested]"
Scan the given directory tree (the current one by default), resolve every spec, and write the
headers and sources. Idempotent: running it twice produces identical files the second time.
.B gen
is an alias for
.BR generate .
.TP
.BI "rename module " "old\-name new\-name"
Rename a module: its spec file and its generated header and source are moved, references are
updated, and the project is regenerated in the same run.
.TP
.BI "fix\-prototypes " "[directory]"
Scan every Pinfit\-generated module source
.RI ( .c )
file in scope for functions written directly inside a usercode region that have no prototype
anywhere in the file. For each file with findings, print a unified diff of the prototype(s) it
would add to the
.I module.source.prototypes
usercode region, and ask for confirmation before writing anything.
.TP
.B detach
.B "DESTRUCTIVE."
Permanently remove Pinfit from the project: keeps generated C code and unrelated YAML, removes the
Pinfit marker lines, then deletes
.IR pinfit.yaml ,
every
.I *.interface.yaml
and
.IR *.module.yaml ,
and the custom documentation YAML the project referenced. Asks for the project name to confirm.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f ", " \-\-force
.B init :
overwrite an existing
.I pinfit.yaml
instead of refusing.
.br
.B generate :
overwrite files on disk that aren't Pinfit\-generated instead of refusing.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
.B generate :
print the project root, scope, and for every output file which spec produced it, whether it's
new or was regenerated, and how many user regions were carried over \- instead of the progress
bar.
.TP
.B \-\-also\-nested
.B generate :
also generate every nested project found under the scanned directory (any subdirectory with its
own
.IR pinfit.yaml ,
normally left alone), each using its own
.I pinfit.yaml
settings. Asks for confirmation after a fast directory count.
.TP
.BI "\-\-implements " "name[,name...]"
.B "create module" :
interfaces the module implements.
.TP
.BI "\-\-interface " "name"
.B "create observer" :
the listener interface. Required.
.TP
.BI "\-\-capacity " "n"
.B "create observer" :
maximum subscribers.
.TP
.BI "\-\-from " "interface"
.B "create adapter" :
the interface it exposes. Required.
.TP
.BI "\-\-to " "interface"
.B "create adapter" :
the interface it calls into. Required.
.TP
.BI "\-\-dir " "directory"
.B create :
the target directory, as an explicit flag instead of a positional argument.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help. Given after a command
.RI ( "pinfit <command> \-\-help" )
it prints that command's usage; given alone it lists all commands.
.TP
.BI "help " "[command]"
Same as
.BR \-\-help ,
also accepted as the first argument:
.B "pinfit help"
lists commands,
.B "pinfit help <command>"
prints that command's usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A
.B "Pinfit error"
was printed \- an invalid spec, a missing reference, a refused overwrite, an unreadable file \-
or a confirmation prompt was declined
.RI ( detach ", " "\-\-also\-nested" ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I pinfit.yaml
Project configuration, created by
.BR "pinfit init" .
.TP
.I *.interface.yaml ", " *.module.yaml
Specs created by
.BR "pinfit create" .
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: https://daoek.github.io/Pinfit/
